Z||000009||FIERO JOHN-WI||07-25-2001||12:41 PM||||Thanks again fiero junky! The first3 pictures are the real pontiac prototype the one after that are mine. I was swapped with e-mails last night about many questions heres the answers: before I do that I don't know why they look so dark? STOCK FIERO MEASURED LAST NIGHT 13FT-5INCH THE FOUR SEATER 16FT-8INCH THIS IS FROM NOSE COVER TO NOSE COVER.<BR>2 FIERO SPACE FRAMES WERE USED<BR>THE FIERO USE 87 SE FRONT & 87 GT AND IS TITLED 87SE IF SOMEONE IS  REALLY INTERESTED<BR>i WILL POST THE VIN TO SHOW THE CAR IS NOT A JUNK CAR AND IS STILL REGISTERED TO ME.<BR>84,000 ORIGINAL MILES ON THE CAR THE FRONT HALF WAS MY DAILY DRIVER UNTIL I PURCHASED BLOWN 87 GT FRAME FROM PAUL VARGYIS.<BR>POWER WINDOWS, LOCKS, MIRRORS(WIRING) 2 SUNROOFS(YES 2!) AUTOMATIC, NO SUB-WOOFER, 88 BEECHWOOD INTERIOR YES POWER LUMBAR DRIVERS SEAT (DON'T HAVE ANY BACK SEATS) COULDN'T FIND A GOOD SET. <BR>iF YOU LOOK AT THE PROTOTYPE IT HAS THE TOUCH TONE STEERING WHEEL, i HAVE THIS AS WELL MOUNTED ON A FIERO COLUMN (ALL IN BLACK)WITH THE RADIO THAT GOES WITH IT.<BR>THE LAST ANSWER TO E-MAIL QUESTION FROM LAST NIGHT. I WANTED TO HAVE IT PAINTED FORESTGREEN (PON. BONNIV.) WITH TAN INTERIOR<BR>AND TO ANSWER TODAYS QUESTION WHY DID I BUILD IT I'M A FIERO FANATIC!<BR>ONE LAST ANSWER IT WILL BE RUNNING AT THE TIME OF SALE JUST FINISHING SODERING THE WIRING HARNESS TOGETHER.<BR>||||reg||1
